<title>JAPAN: Japan's Ikeda to attend H.Kong handover ceremony.</title>
<headline>Japan's Ikeda to attend H.Kong handover ceremony.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese Foreign Minister Yukihiko Ikeda will attend the ceremony marking the British colony's handover to China next week, the Foreign Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>Ikeda will leave Japan on Sunday for a four-day visit to Hong Kong. He is also scheduled to meet Chinese Foreign Minister Qian Qichen for talks on Monday morning, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Hong Kong reverts to Chinese rule at midnight on Monday June 30.</p>
</text>
